Changelog
---------------------------------
3.0.0 (in development)
    - Complete rewrite: Svelte 5 + TypeScript on Manifest V3
    - New side panel: the issue list now sits alongside whatever you are working on
    - Full view: clicking an issue now opens it beside the list rather than
      leaving for Redmine, which moves to its own icon on each row
    - Full view: start and stop a timer from the issue list
    - Copy an issue's link from the list or from the issue itself
    - Time tracking finally reaches Redmine: stopping a timer logs a real time
      entry, and sessions that fail to send are queued rather than lost
    - Time tracked in 1.x is migrated into that queue on upgrade
    - Editable priority and assignee, alongside status, tracker, % done and estimate
    - Issue history now renders every field, including target version, dates,
      parent, relations and custom fields
    - Fixed: issue text was rendered as HTML, so markup in a subject or comment
      could run inside the extension
    - Fixed: unread state was lost whenever an issue was refetched, and the
      unread counter drifted from the real count
    - Fixed: the cached issue list grew without limit
    - Polling now asks only for issues changed since the last check, instead of
      re-reading every assigned issue every five minutes
    - Connection problems are now reported specifically: a rejected key, a
      disabled REST API and an unreachable host no longer all read as "Err"
    - Host access is requested for your Redmine only, not for every site
    - The API key is stored locally instead of being synced to your Google account
    - Dark mode
    - Dropped ChiliProject support (archived upstream since 2015)

1.6.5 ()
    - Added config synchronization between devices

1.6.0 (15-Feb-2013)
    - Updated Twitter Bootstrap to version 2.3
    - Added ChiliProject support
    - Updated UI
    - Latest news
    - Code optimization and stability improvements

